From 33563a7341b6393bf50246c25ab7acb18c31da5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:38:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add standalone V2 ordinary transaction candidate validation

Check P01 framing and unique spend resolution against an explicit development UTXO view; enforce contextual height/time locks and coinbase maturity, checked u128 native/token conservation, one mint per positive token delta, and the separate P05 byte and C14a token-output fee floors. Execute every selected spend/mint witness through the charged VM and reject invalid or unsupported results. Stage all effects and swap an isolated state copy only after validation passes.

Pin signed compiler fungible-token mint and transfer fixture bytes with source SHA-256. Native Debug and Release tests cover inflation, duplicate spends and mints, wrong resolved Coin, underfee, token floor, missing/mismatched mint, bad VM/proof and second required branch, mint coin-introspection, locks/maturity, and failure atomicity. This is a review model: it does not compute complete transaction-wide P05 L(tx), parabolic block burn, block ordering, persistent chainstate, or block state commitments.
